{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Let us make man.</b> It does not say 'נברא אדם,' for creation was by HaShem alone, as it is written, ״ויברא את האדם״, and He says, ״האדם אשר בראתי״. But the making and the preparation — He associated them with Him, for they were all made there as companions. Another interpretation: <b>Let us make man.</b> Elsewhere too we find a singular speaker using plural language: ״את מי אשלח ומי ילך לנו״, and ״דנא חלמא ופשריה נאמר קדם מלכא״." "<b>Let us make man.</b> אומינ״א in the vernacular. That is: let us make male and female. Proof of this: ״ויקרא את שמם אדם ביום הבראם״. And furthermore, we find: Rav Huna said, where do we find that Eve was called אדם? As it is written, ״כתפארת אדם לשבת בית״ — and we translate it: like the praise of a woman who sits in her house. And furthermore it is written, ״ונפש אדם מן הנשים״." "<b>In our image.</b> In the image of the angels." "<b>Like our likeness.</b> Like the likeness of the angels, and being created in that likeness will avail him to rule over <b>the fish of the sea and the bird</b> etc. Another interpretation: <b>like our likeness</b> — like the likeness of HaShem, may one not say so, for it is written ״ומה דמות תערכו לו״. And if you say: ״בצלמנו כדמותנו״ is like His likeness, in the image that He forms His creatures — if so, what need is there for Scripture to say ״שופך דם האדם״ etc. ״כי בצלם אלקים עשה את האדם״ — what is its novelty? Likewise, בצלם אלקים He made the beast. Rather, perforce <b>in our image, like our likeness</b> means: in our manner, just as I rule over you, so shall he rule over all the lower beings." "<b>And in all the earth.</b> What did Scripture leave unmentioned that it needed to mention this? Rather, it comes to include every such thing — for example: winds, shedim, angels, constellations, luminaries."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {1 "The gloss אומינ״א is left in its original transliterated form as in the source; its precise vernacular referent is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:19:55.256977724Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}